Yes. After searching the current 2026 ecosystem, I think there are **far more interesting API niches than just MCP directories**.

A major signal is that the plumbing is standardizing. MCP now has an official registry designed as a source of truth that other registries can build on; A2A is being used for cross-agent delegation; Coinbase's x402 lets an agent discover and purchase an API call in the HTTP request flow; and a July 2026 IETF draft proposes `/.well-known/ai` so websites can advertise capabilities directly to agents. ([Model Context Protocol Blog][1])

That means I would **not** spend most of your time making wrappers. Build intelligence *over* this emerging machine web.

