# 1. API Price Intelligence

This is actually bigger than LLM Deals.

There is already work trying to make API pricing and rate limits machine-readable: API Evangelist reports generating pricing, rate-limit and FinOps artifacts across **3,837 API providers**. ([API Evangelist][2])

That tells me the raw problem is real.

Build:

```text
api-prices.org

GET /provider
GET /product
GET /pricing
GET /quota
GET /rate-limits
GET /changes
GET /promotions
POST /estimate
POST /cheapest
```

Normalize:

```json
{
  "service": "example",
  "operation": "search",
  "unit": "request",
  "price": 0.001,
  "free_allowance": 1000,
  "rate_limit": {},
  "promotion": null,
  "observed_at": "...",
  "source": "...",
  "confidence": 0.99
}
```

Then an agent can ask:

> Find the cheapest currently operational search API that can return 100 results for <$0.01.

That's far more useful than a price-comparison website.

